            <ArticleTitle>[Abdominal tuberculosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>257-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Abdominal tuberculosis develops according to a non-specific clinical picture, with a difficult differential diagnosis with respect to other entities of similar semiology. We present the case of a male who was admitted because of abdominal pain, progressive and notable loss of body weight and a fever of two months evolution. The culture from the colon biopsy showed the presence of Koch bacilli.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
